Core/Jessie: You said this started with food, right? Fruits and vegetables?
Core/Rose: Yeah. Infected insects pollinating crops. The pathogens spread through the plants themselves.
Core/Jessie: So… anyone who ate them…
Core/Rose: Became a carrier. But it took days for symptoms to show. Sometimes a week.
Core/Jessie: Long enough for it to spread everywhere.
Core/Rose: Exactly. By the time people started getting sick, half the country had already eaten contaminated produce.
Core/Jessie: God, that’s… efficient.
Core/Rose: Nature’s good at that.